    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0282" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg270"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.9111/38: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-07T12:00:00+03:25">February 7,
                            1942—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 3:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. Department’s 26, February 5.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d309-f1"/> Immediately
                    upon receipt Department’s 19, January 26,<anchor n="58" xml:id="d309-f2"/> I
                    handed the Foreign Minister a note which conveyed the reservation of rights and
                    requested the desired assurance. Foreign Minister promised early reply but
                    stated matter was technical and would require study. He added that while he did
                    not understand the points involved he was always glad to have an expression of
                    American interest in Iran’s problems.</p>
                <p>Before delivering note I ascertained from British Minister that he had informed
                    Iranian Government of American participation along lines suggested in
                    Department’s 166, December 30.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d309-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
